{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The closure the rider herself accepts is documented, and it clears the first 3.60 km of excess on the driver's side. LTA advisory EV-ADVIS-09113-01 is a HIGH-severity CLOSURE of the 'Pelton Canal Link eastbound connector' — the very segment the booking-time optimal route traverses, as the trip record's optimal_route_source confirms ('routing-engine-v3.2 snapshot 2026-09-20 18:12 SGT via Pelton Canal Link, the segment named in the LTA advisory'). The advisory runs 18:14–18:55 and so brackets the trip window of 18:20–18:54 well inside the 15-minute buffer POL-RD-03 allows at each end, and the completed trace leaves the closed corridor and rejoins it. Under POL-RD-03 the justified excess is the lesser of the measured 8.0 km and 1.30 x (12.0 km shortest lawful alternative - 10.0 km booked optimal) + 1.00 km tolerance = 3.60 km. So 3.60 km of the excess is exonerated as an external event and is not the driver's to refund.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-09113-01", "EV-TRIP-09113", "EV-GPS-09113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money.closure[0].justified_excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's recovery is the arithmetic refund against the closure-adjusted optimal route, not against the booked 10.0 km route. POL-RD-03 sets the closure-adjusted optimal at 10.0 + 3.60 = 13.60 km, with duration scaled to 27.2 minutes, and POL-RD-02 then gives recomputed fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 13.60 + 0.28 x 27.2) x 1.0 surge multiplier read from the fare breakdown + 0.80 platform fee + 1.00 ERP for the on-optimal-route Pelton gantry = 23.416, against a charged_total of 31.42. The refund is therefore 8.004, payable 8.05 after rounding up to the nearest SGD 0.05, which is the ceiling of the rider's recovery on this record. An unadjusted computation against the booked optimal would produce 12.75 and is the wrong baseline on this evidence.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09113", "EV-TRIP-09113", "EV-GPS-09113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money.closure[0].refund.payable",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The 2.80 'Industrial loop exit' ERP line, flagged on_optimal_route false, is already comprehended inside that 8.05 refund and must never be added on top of it. POL-RD-02 recomputes the fare including only the gantries lying on the optimal route, and the only such line here is the 1.00 'Pelton lawful diversion entry' charge, which the recomputed fare of 23.416 already carries; the 3.80 total ERP billed against a 1.00 on-route pass-through is precisely where the difference sits. POL-RD-09(1) forbids counting an off-route pass-through a second time, so the rider cannot come away with 8.05 plus 2.80.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09113", "EV-GPS-09113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.erp_lines",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no repeat-deviation pattern on this driver and therefore no uplift. driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 610, which satisfies neither limb of the POL-RD-06 test — not '3 or more flags', and not the 0.05 ratio with at least 40 trips. Those two fields are the only ones POL-RD-06 permits for this test, and neither supports escalation to the FULL_REFUND remedy or the POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral; the rider's remedy stays at the POL-RD-02 partial figure of 8.05.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-09113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider authorised the diversion as it happened. The chat log records the driver messaging at 18:22:40, two minutes into the trip, that the Pelton Canal Link closure was sending traffic around the industrial loop, and the rider replying at 18:23:10, 'Understood, please take the lawful diversion' — an instruction from the rider, in the chat log, inside the three minutes after the vehicle left the optimal corridor that POL-RD-04 allows. I disclose that the rider named no road and the message carries no waypoint_hint, so the 200 m waypoint-corroboration limb of POL-RD-04 cannot be run on this record; the exchange is relied on as the rider's authorisation of the diversion the driver had just identified, which is why the industrial-loop routing cannot be treated as the driver's unilateral choice.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-09113", "EV-GPS-09113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "relies_on": "chat_log.messages[1].sent_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver has discharged the burden POL-RD-08 places on him once the rider shows an excess: he points to a specific artifact and a specific clause — traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-09113-01 and POL-RD-03 — rather than a general assertion that traffic was bad. The advisory names the road, carries an ID, overlaps the trip window and matches a route that leaves and rejoins the optimal corridor, which is exactly what POL-RD-08 requires. The excess is also stable and admissible: the governing figure is the trace distance of 18.0 km under POL-RD-01, the trace is at full weight with no gaps, so the 3.60 km cap does not move and the rider cannot inflate the measured excess beyond it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-09113-01", "EV-GPS-09113", "EV-TRIP-09113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 9.05,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing integrity: the SGD 1.00 'Pelton lawful diversion entry' ERP line is unmatched to the GPS trace (nearest fix 834 m against the clause's 250 m match radius) and is refunded in full as a standalone correction; record the finding against the fare ledger."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the rider is substantially right, and the driver is exonerated only to the capped extent the closure justifies.\n\nDeviation is established on this trip's own trace (POL-RD-01). The governing figure is gps_trace.trace_distance_km = 18.0 km, not the trip record's rounded copy; against the booked optimal of 10.0 km that is an excess of 8.0 km, or 80%, so both gates (over 20% and over 0.8 km) are cleared and the excess is additionally MATERIAL. That required the POL-RD-06 driver-profile check, which is negative: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 610 completed trips in 90 days, so neither limb of the pattern test is met and there is no FULL_REFUND uplift and no conduct referral. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07(a)-(c): 205 fixes at a 10-second interval, zero gaps, 100% coverage, so no corroboration substitute and no POL-RD-10(3) escalation arise.\n\nThe Pelton Canal Link closure (EV-ADVIS-09113-01, LTA) is real, names the segment the booked optimal route uses, overlaps the trip window and matches a route that leaves and rejoins the corridor, so POL-RD-03 exoneration applies - but only up to its cap. Justified excess = min(8.0, 1.30 x (12.0 - 10.0) + 1.00) = 3.60 km, giving a closure-adjusted optimal of 13.60 km at 27.2 minutes. The remaining 4.4 km of excess is the driver's.\n\nPOL-RD-04 does not reduce that further. The rider's message 'Understood, please take the lawful diversion' names no road and carries waypoint_hint null, so the corroboration test cannot be run and the clause is unavailable; the exchange is context, not an exclusion of distance. POL-RD-02 therefore runs against the closure-adjusted route: (3.80 + 0.75 x 13.60 + 0.28 x 27.2) x 1.0 surge multiplier read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier + 0.80 platform fee + 1.00 on-optimal-route ERP = 23.416; refund = 31.42 charged_total - 23.416 = 8.004, rounded up to 8.05. That is above the 0.50 de minimis floor and below the 90% full-refund share, so the outcome is partial, not full and not nil.\n\nOn the ERP lines, the rider's assertion that 'both ERP gantries are matched within the 250 m radius' is rejected: the 'Industrial loop exit' line sits 223 m from the trace and is matched, but the 'Pelton lawful diversion entry' line's nearest fix is 834 m, far outside the 250 m match radius POL-RD-09(4) applies. That line is a billing-integrity failure and is refunded in full as a standalone correction of 1.00, on top of the 8.05 - it is not the off-route line, so POL-RD-09(1) does not already comprehend it. The 2.80 'Industrial loop exit' line is off-optimal-route and IS already comprehended in the 8.05 recomputation and is not added a second time. Because the only unmatched line is one refunded under POL-RD-09(4), POL-RD-10(8) is not triggered and no escalation follows; total refund is therefore 8.05 + 1.00 = 9.05. All artifacts relied on carry weight_multiplier 1.0, so no discount applies and no impairment narration is required."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
